Task: Add a Dockerfile and pin dependencies for a FastAPI ML service.

Stack: Python 3.12, managed with uv (has a pyproject.toml + uv.lock). Dependencies currently use >= ranges in pyproject.toml (e.g. fastapi>=0.141.1, xgboost>=3.4.1) — need these pinned to exact versions for reproducible builds, since uv.lock already resolves exact versions but the pyproject.toml itself doesn't reflect that.

App structure:

api.py — FastAPI app, entrypoint is uvicorn api:app, exposes /health and POST /predict
config.py — shared config/threshold loading
feature_engineering_telco.py — feature transform, imported by api.py
xgboost_churn_pipeline.pkl and model_metadata.json — trained model artifacts the app loads at startup via a FastAPI lifespan handler (these are gitignored/generated by a notebook, not committed — the Docker image needs to either copy them in at build time or expect them mounted/provided at runtime)
pyproject.toml has a [dependency-groups] dev group (pytest, httpx) that should NOT be installed in the production image — only the base [project] dependencies

What I need:

A Dockerfile that uses uv to install locked/pinned production dependencies only (excluding the dev group), copies in the app code, and runs uvicorn api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000. Should be a slim multi-stage build if reasonable.
Guidance/edits to pin pyproject.toml's dependencies to exact versions (not >= ranges) so the image is reproducible — ideally derived from what's already resolved in uv.lock rather than picked arbitrarily.
Flag whether the model artifacts (.pkl/.json) should be baked into the image or mounted as a volume, given they're currently gitignored.